      "beat_id": "B01",
      "act": "TITLE",
      "narration_text": "Namaste — this is Liam, in for Ameya. Why the language model is almost the whole clock, in ninety seconds.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "motion": "fade",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B01",
          "file": "scenes.py"
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 7.85,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim\\B01.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B01",
        "at": "2026-09-07T22:25:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "act": "STATEMENT",
      "narration_text": "A model writes one token, then runs the whole network again for the next. A hundred tokens is a hundred passes, in strict sequence. That's why it's slow.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "motion": "fade",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B02",
          "file": "scenes.py"
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 8.94,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim\\B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B02",
        "at": "2026-09-07T22:25:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "act": "STATEMENT",
      "narration_text": "The key-value cache stores every past token so each step only computes the newest one. It turns a quadratic cost into a linear one — for memory.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "motion": "fade",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B03",
          "file": "scenes.py"
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.11,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim\\B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B03",
        "at": "2026-09-07T22:25:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "act": "LIST",
      "narration_text": "To go faster: batch requests for throughput, quantize the weights for cheaper hardware, and let a draft model propose tokens the big one verifies at once.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "motion": "fade",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B04",
          "file": "scenes.py"
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 9.0,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim\\B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B04",
        "at": "2026-09-07T22:25:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "act": "STATEMENT",
      "narration_text": "The cheapest win: stream the tokens. Total time is the same, but the user sees words in two hundred milliseconds instead of two seconds.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "manim",
        "motion": "fade",
        "manim": {
          "scene_class": "B05",
          "file": "scenes.py"
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B05.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 8.26,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim\\B05.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim:B05",
        "at": "2026-09-07T22:25:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "act": "STATEMENT",
      "narration_text": "And optimise the big number. In the project the model was over a thousand milliseconds; vector search was two tenths of a percent.",
      "shot": {
